  "note": "Round 2 (nested cross-validation, motion correction, Friston-24 + FD scrubbing, high-variance confounds). Best 3-class model is Logistic regression at balanced accuracy 0.50 (accuracy 0.53, AUC 0.58) on Schaefer-100 parcels \u2014 atlas100 best balanced accuracy 0.50; atlas200 best balanced accuracy 0.44. Binary HC-vs-PD on this atlas: SVM (RBF) AUC 0.44, balanced accuracy 0.51 \u2014 lower than the first round's 0.74 AUC, because proper motion and noise cleaning removed signal that turned out to be noise, not brain activity (see the model card). The best binary model overall is XGBoost on Schaefer-200 (AUC 0.69). Two-stage (HC-vs-PD, then PD-NC-vs-PD-MCI) with logistic regression: combined balanced accuracy 0.40. Chance is 0.33 for 3-class. Full logs, confusion matrices and model card are in the GitHub repository. Research demo only \u2014 not a medical diagnosis.",
